# CREDENTIALS.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds DEMO credentials that
# RoleBasedUsersSeeder generates (@test.com / password123), AGENTS.md points
# developers at it, and a clean clone needs it to log in. It sat in this file
# for months, which is why nobody reviewed it and three of its fifteen rows
# rotted into usernames that never existed. It is safe to track because
# CredentialsDocumentationTest now fails when the document and the seeder
# disagree in EITHER direction — a real secret could not be added there
# without breaking the build.
